Description: Add extraContainers and extraInitContainers hooks
 Gentian syncs an app's git-managed content with upstream git-sync running
 INSIDE the app's pod, writing an emptyDir the app container also mounts. That
 needs somewhere to inject the containers, and this chart offers no hook.
 .
 Without it the sync has to run as a separate Deployment writing a shared
 ReadWriteMany volume, which makes a StorageClass with RWX a hard requirement
 for an app whose content is a few MB of public, reproducible git. Most
 clusters have no such class -- block storage (Cinder, EBS) is ReadWriteOnce --
 so the PVC never binds and every pod mounting it is unschedulable.
 .
 Additive and guarded by 'if', in the same style as 0004: with the values unset
 the rendered output is byte-identical to upstream.
Author: Gentian Platform <platform@gentian.org>
Origin: other, https://github.com/gentian-org/gentian-apps
Forwarded: no
Bug-Upstream: none filed
Reason: Gentian-specific extension points, the same generic 'extra*' convention
 0004 introduced; worth proposing upstream, but not a defect report.
Applied-Upstream: no
Last-Update: 2026-08-28
---
--- a/templates/_podSpec.tpl
+++ b/templates/_podSpec.tpl
@@ -34,6 +34,10 @@
       {{- end }}
     serviceAccountName: {{ include "activepieces.serviceAccountName" . }}
     automountServiceAccountToken: {{ .Values.serviceAccount.automount }}
+    {{- if .Values.extraInitContainers }}
+    initContainers:
+      {{- toYaml .Values.extraInitContainers | nindent 6 }}
+    {{- end }}
     containers:
       - name: {{ .Chart.Name }}
         image: {{ include "activepieces.image" . }}
@@ -176,6 +180,9 @@
           successThreshold: {{ .Values.startupProbe.successThreshold }}
           failureThreshold: {{ .Values.startupProbe.failureThreshold }}
         {{- end }}
+      {{- if .Values.extraContainers }}
+      {{- toYaml .Values.extraContainers | nindent 6 }}
+      {{- end }}
     {{- if .Values.priorityClassName }}
     priorityClassName: {{ .Values.priorityClassName }}
     {{- end }}
